.TH HU20CTL 1 "November 2026" "hu20ctl 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hu20ctl \- technical control CLI and capture daemon for SecuGen Hamster Pro 20 (HU20)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hu20ctl
[\fIGLOBAL_OPTIONS\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGUMENTS...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hu20ctl
is a pure-Rust command-line tool and background daemon for technical and forensic
operations on the SecuGen Hamster Pro 20 (HU20) optical fingerprint scanner
(USB 1162:2200, 300x400 L8 @ 500 DPI, 120,000 bytes).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B completions install bash|zsh|fish|powershell
Install shell completion for the current user. Creates needed directories and
updates the selected shell's startup configuration. Open a new terminal to use it.
.TP
.B doctor
Run hardware, udev, permission, and daemon diagnostics.
.TP
.B list
List connected SecuGen HU20 scanners on the USB bus.
.TP
.B capture
Acquire a fingerprint frame and write PNG, TIFF, PGM, RAW, WSQ, JP2, JPEG, or BMP.
.TP
.B enroll
Acquire multiple samples and produce a deterministic enrollment template.
.TP
.B verify
Verify a probe image/template against a reference image/template (1:1 or 1:N).
.TP
.B daemon
Run the exclusive-access Unix Domain Socket capture daemon.
.TP
.B tool
Offline utilities: \fBbench\fR, \fBconvert\fR, \fBenhance\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B HU20_MOCK_FIXTURE
Select a mock scenario (\fBmatch\fR, \fBmismatch\fR, \fBdegraded\fR, \fBempty\fR, \fBdisconnect\fR).
.TP
.B HU20_SOCKET_PATH
Override the Unix Domain Socket path (default: \fI/run/hu20/hu20.sock\fR on Linux, \fI/tmp/hu20.sock\fR on macOS).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR udev (7),
.BR systemd (1)

.SH CONFIGURATION
Use config init to create a private TOML configuration without overwriting files.
Linux uses $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/hu20ctl/config.toml (absolute paths only), falling back
to $HOME/.config/hu20ctl/config.toml. macOS uses
$HOME/Library/Application Support/hu20ctl/config.toml.
.PP
--config PATH selects a file; --no-config disables loading. Explicit CLI arguments
override supported environment variables, file values, then built-in defaults.
config path, config show, and config validate report paths, effective values with
origins, and validity as JSON. schema_version must be 1; unknown keys are errors.
.PP
Supported sections: capture (timeout_secs, min_quality), enroll (samples,
timeout_secs, min_quality), verify (threshold), forensic (comparison_threshold),
conversion (wsq_bitrate, dpi for tool convert), driver (poll_interval_ms), and
daemon (absolute socket_path). Restart the daemon after editing configuration.
